[FINDING] 2026-09-03 MINOR technical parity — story-prophet-musa.html:294 is missing data-ar and also breaks the established phrasing pattern used by every sibling story page:
  `<a href="story-prophet-yusuf.html" class="nav-btn next">Another Story: Prophet Yusuf →</a>`
  Compare story-prophet-nuh.html:250 `data-ar="القصة التالية: النبي يوسف"` and story-prophet-ibrahim.html:404 `data-ar="القصة التالية: النبي نوح"` which both use "القصة التالية: النبي X" ("Next Story: Prophet X"). Musa's English also drifts to "Another Story:" instead of "Next Story:" — recommend aligning English to the pattern too, then adding data-ar="القصة التالية: النبي يوسف".

[FINDING] 2026-09-03 MINOR escaping/fragility — index.html:43 and ayat-al-kursi.html:330-331 double-escape HTML entities inside data-ar: `&amp;mdash;` and `&amp;nbsp;` (should be `&mdash;` / `&nbsp;`). Verified this currently renders correctly by accident: the browser decodes the attribute once at parse time (turning `&amp;mdash;` into the literal text "&mdash;"), then bilingual.js's `el.innerHTML = el.getAttribute('data-ar')` parses that literal text a second time as HTML, which decodes "&mdash;" into an actual em dash. So there is no live visual bug today, but the mechanism only works because of this double-decode coincidence — if the swap logic is ever changed to use textContent (e.g. for XSS-safety hardening) these will start rendering as the literal string "&mdash;"/"&nbsp;" in Arabic mode. Recommend fixing to single-escaped `&mdash;`/`&nbsp;` for robustness, or just using the literal — / non-breaking space characters directly.

[FINDING] 2026-09-03 MINOR digit consistency — surah-fatiha.html:304, surah-al-ikhlas.html:264, ayat-al-kursi.html:319 render the quiz score with `data-ar="أجبت <span id=&quot;scoreDisplay&quot;>0</span> من ٤ إجابات صحيحة!"` — the "٤" (total) is correctly Arabic-Indic, but surah.js:110 sets `scoreDisplay.textContent = score` with a plain JS number, so the live score will always render as a Western digit (e.g. "3") sitting next to the Arabic-Indic "٤" — "أجبت 3 من ٤ إجابات صحيحة!". Same likely true for story-prophet-nuh.html:217 (`من ٣ إجابات`) if its scoring code is shared. Minor but visible on every completed quiz in Arabic mode. Everywhere else in the site, Arabic-Indic digits (٠-٩) and Western digits are used consistently and deliberately — Arabic-Indic in all data-ar prose/badges, Western only inside transliteration and untranslated JS placeholders — so this quiz-score spot is the one real inconsistency found.

[FINDING] 2026-09-03 MINOR typography — the whole site (English and Arabic alike) uses straight ASCII quotation marks via `&quot;` for every quoted dua/hadith/Quran translation (e.g. surah-al-ikhlas.html:75,89,90; story-prophet-nuh.html:83,163,261). Not a bug — it is applied consistently on both sides — but Arabic typographic convention favours «guillemets» or “curly” quotes for quoted speech, especially for Quranic/hadith quotations read aloud to a child. Cosmetic; flagging as a polish opportunity, not a fix-now item.

